# LF everywhere, in the index and in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this file, core.autocrlf=true checks text out as CRLF on Windows while the index
# holds LF. The index stayed clean, but 15 working-tree files had drifted to CRLF, and the
# drift is invisible in a diff -- which is exactly why it needs a rule rather than a habit.
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf, so a machine with it set still gets LF here.
#
# Enforced on every gate run by `linebreak-style` in @repo/eslint-config, which covers the
# source. This file covers everything else: markdown, JSON, YAML, CSS.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zst binary
